        "Architected and deployed the Automated Indicator Sharing (AIS) anomaly detection platform using ensemble methods (Random Forest, XGBoost, deep autoencoders), reducing mean time to detect advanced persistent threats from 78 days to 11 days across 102 federal agencies",
        "Designed and implemented a graph neural network (GNN) pipeline for lateral movement detection, achieving 94.2% precision and 91.7% recall on classified validation datasets, directly contributing to the identification of 3 nation-state intrusion campaigns in FY2023",
        "Led the migration of legacy analytics infrastructure from on-premises Hadoop clusters to AWS GovCloud (IL-5), reducing compute costs by 34% ($2.1M annual savings) while increasing processing throughput by 4.7x",
        "Developed Natural Language Processing models for automated analysis of 450,000+ vulnerability disclosures annually, enabling prioritized patch guidance to critical infrastructure sectors within 48 hours of disclosure",
        "Authored 14 technical white papers and Intelligence Community Directives (ICDs) establishing data science standards and best practices for cyber threat intelligence analytics across DHS component agencies",
        "Represented CISA at the National Security Council’s Cyber Directorate, providing technical briefings on AI/ML capabilities for national cyber defense to senior government officials including the National Cyber Director",
        "Established and chair the DHS Data Science Working Group (47 members across 6 component agencies), driving standardization of ML model governance, bias testing, and deployment protocols",
        "Mentored 6 junior data scientists (GS-9 through GS-12) through the CISA Data Science Development Program, with 4 achieving promotion within 18 months",
        "Developed an insider threat behavioral analytics model integrating 23 data sources (badge access, network logs, email metadata, financial disclosures) achieving AUC of 0.96, adopted by 3 additional federal agencies",
        "Coordinated with NSA, FBI Cyber Division, and US-CERT on joint analytical products, authoring 8 Joint Analysis Reports (JARs) disseminated to critical infrastructure owners and operators",
        "Implemented MLOps pipelines using Kubeﬂow on classified infrastructure, reducing model deployment time from 6 weeks to 3 days and enabling continuous model retraining on streaming threat data",
        "Presented research findings at classified and unclassified venues including the NSA Cybersecurity Symposium, the DHS Science and Technology Conference, and the Intelligence Community Data Science Summit"
